# purpose
Leave requests get lost in email, and nobody knows who approved what.
requests decided within two days, up
Every leave request is decided by the right person. Nobody approves their own.
# people and things
employee: asks for time off; manager: approves or refuses requests; hr: approves long requests
Leave request: a request for time off | days: integer
# an example, then the actions in your words
LR-7: days 12
request_leave: Ask for time off -> new Leave request; approve_leave: Approve the request -> Leave request; reject_leave: Refuse the request -> Leave request
# who may (three actions), the limit, who must not: the recommended choices
 
 
 
 
 
# stages, then each action's column and the outcome rule: recommended
status: submitted, approved, rejected; starts submitted
 
 
 
# invariants: nothing beyond the stages
nothing
# world
employee: eli; manager: mia; hr: hana
employee request_leave LR-9 days=3 -> submitted; manager approve_leave LR-9 -> approved; manager approve_leave LR-9 -> refused
# handoffs: none
none
# review: confirm
yes
